---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Customer Success & Customer Operations" current="/customer-success/" description="Richard Allen's experience in customer success, customer experience, SaaS support, technical support, training, people management, customer journeys, and customer operations.">
<section class="role-hero cx-hero"><div class="container role-hero-grid">
  <div class="role-hero-copy">
    <div class="eyebrow light">Customer Success & Customer Operations</div>
    <h1>See the whole customer relationship—not just the next ticket.</h1>
    <p>My customer-facing work combines relationship management, SaaS and technical support, people leadership, training, escalation management, customer feedback, reporting, and the operating discipline needed to make service clearer and more consistent.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button button-light" href="/case-studies/">See customer-facing case studies</a><a class="role-hero-link" href="/resume/">View résumé →</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="lifecycle-panel" aria-label="Customer lifecycle from discovery through adoption, support, growth, and retention">
    <div class="lifecycle-title">CUSTOMER LIFECYCLE</div>
    <div class="lifecycle-track">
      <div><span>01</span><strong>Discover</strong><small>first contact</small></div>
      <i>→</i><div><span>02</span><strong>Adopt</strong><small>onboarding & use</small></div>
      <i>→</i><div><span>03</span><strong>Support</strong><small>service & troubleshooting</small></div>
      <i>→</i><div><span>04</span><strong>Grow</strong><small>value & education</small></div>
      <i>→</i><div><span>05</span><strong>Retain</strong><small>continuity & loyalty</small></div>
    </div>
    <div class="journey-proof"><strong>~26</strong><span>cross-functional participants in year-long Customer Journey / Customer Lifeline work</span></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="cx-proof-band"><div class="container cx-proof-grid" aria-label="Selected customer success scope">
  <div><strong>6 yrs</strong><span>HawkSoft customer and technical support experience</span></div>
  <div><strong>32</strong><span>support & technical-support representatives managed</span></div>
  <div><strong>Hundreds</strong><span>of Kotter customers personally contacted to assess experience</span></div>
  <div><strong>1+ yr</strong><span>co-leading cross-functional customer-journey work</span></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section cx-loop-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Customer operating loop</div><h2>Listen, solve, enable, and feed the learning back into the system.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Strong customer operations connect the immediate issue to the larger patterns behind it.</p></div>
  <div class="feedback-loop" aria-label="Customer feedback loop from listening through support, training, improvement, and relationship continuity">
    <div class="loop-stage listen"><span>LISTEN</span><strong>Customer voice</strong><small>feedback · surveys · conversations</small></div>
    <i>→</i><div class="loop-stage solve"><span>SOLVE</span><strong>Support & escalation</strong><small>troubleshoot · coordinate · resolve</small></div>
    <i>→</i><div class="loop-stage enable"><span>ENABLE</span><strong>Training & adoption</strong><small>documentation · webinars · guidance</small></div>
    <i>→</i><div class="loop-stage improve"><span>IMPROVE</span><strong>Process & product insight</strong><small>patterns · reporting · recommendations</small></div>
    <i>↺</i><div class="loop-stage retain"><span>RELATIONSHIP</span><strong>Retention & trust</strong><small>clearer service · stronger continuity</small></div>
  </div>
  <div class="cx-highlight"><div><span>THE KOTTER GROUP</span><strong>Built the operating home for customer experience.</strong></div><p>Established and managed the Customer Experience / Customer Success function, maintained relationships across the client base, personally contacted hundreds of customers, gathered survey and conversational feedback, resolved issues, and created customer education and communications.</p></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section cx-evidence-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Customer-facing proof</div><h2>Where relationships, systems, and operations meet.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Selected examples from HawkSoft, The Kotter Group, and related customer-operations work.</p></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid cx-card-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">TEAM</div><h3>Support management & coaching</h3><p>At HawkSoft, managed 21 people as Team Lead before promotion to Customer Support Manager in 2015, then managed 32 Customer Support and Technical Support representatives, not including four team leads. Work included hiring and disciplinary authority, performance management, workflow coverage, escalations, quality review, stand-ups, and one-on-one coaching.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">SaaS</div><h3>Technical support & adoption</h3><p>Supported insurance-agency customers using HawkSoft CMS, trained customers and staff on software features and workflows, handled complex escalations, and coordinated customer database and hosted-service transitions.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">CX</div><h3>Customer Journey leadership</h3><p>Co-led a cross-functional Customer Journey / Customer Lifeline initiative for about a year with approximately 26 participants, mapping customer touchpoints across the relationship and helping teams identify handoffs, friction, and retention opportunities beyond their own departments.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">BUILD</div><h3>Building a Customer Experience function</h3><p>At The Kotter Group, established and managed a Customer Experience / Customer Success function, maintained relationships across the client base, gathered feedback, resolved issues, and supported service improvement and retention.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">LEARN</div><h3>Training & customer education</h3><p>Created training documentation, presentations, webinars, online content, and customer communications at The Kotter Group. At HawkSoft, created and participated in training for a major accounting-software redesign and trained customers and staff on troubleshooting, workflows, product changes, and best practices.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">DATA</div><h3>Service reporting & pattern recognition</h3><p>Built operational and management reporting from support and call data, turning large Excel exports into information leadership could use for staffing, training, procedure, policy, and service decisions.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section tight"><div class="container"><div class="fit-banner"><strong>Best-fit customer-facing work</strong><span>Customer operations · customer success leadership · enablement · onboarding · implementation support · service operations · training · CX improvement</span><small>Best when the focus is improving the system—not personally carrying a high-volume phone queue.</small></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/case-studies/">See case studies</a><a class="button secondary" href="/resume/">View résumé</a><a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Contact</a></div></div></section>

<style>
  .role-hero{padding:4.8rem 0 4rem;color:#fff;overflow:hidden}.cx-hero{background:radial-gradient(circle at 82% 16%,rgba(43,108,176,.38),transparent 28%),linear-gradient(128deg,#102f55 0%,#174c7e 58%,#126b73 100%)}.role-hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(420px,1fr);gap:3rem;align-items:center}.role-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,6vw,5rem);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:.7rem 0 1.25rem}.role-hero p{font-size:1.15rem;color:#e2edf5;max-width:720px}.role-hero-link{color:#fff;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;align-self:center}.role-hero-link:hover{color:#d2fff8}.lifecycle-panel{padding:1.2rem;border-radius:24px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);box-shadow:0 24px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.2)}.lifecycle-title{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.15em;color:#c8e7f8;margin:.2rem 0 1rem}.lifecycle-track{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;align-items:center;gap:.35rem}.lifecycle-track>div{min-height:125px;padding:.75rem .5rem;border-radius:15px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.09);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;text-align:center}.lifecycle-track span{width:28px;height:28px;margin:0 auto .45rem;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;background:rgba(255,255,255,.13);font-size:.66rem;font-weight:900}.lifecycle-track strong{font-size:.92rem}.lifecycle-track small{color:#d9e6ef;font-size:.72rem;margin-top:.2rem}.lifecycle-track>i{font-style:normal;color:#8eb1c9}.journey-proof{margin-top:.8rem;padding:.85rem 1rem;border-radius:14px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.8rem}.journey-proof strong{font-size:1.8rem;color:#9de5dc}.journey-proof span{font-size:.83rem;color:#dbe8f0;line-height:1.35}.cx-proof-band{background:#fff;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.cx-proof-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)}.cx-proof-grid>div{padding:1.35rem;border-right:1px solid var(--border)}.cx-proof-grid>div:last-child{border-right:0}.cx-proof-grid strong{display:block;font-size:2rem;line-height:1;color:var(--accent-2)}.cx-proof-grid span{display:block;margin-top:.4rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.35}.cx-loop-section{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#f4f9fd,#fff)}.feedback-loop{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;gap:.45rem;align-items:center}.loop-stage{min-height:160px;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;background:#fff;box-shadow:0 10px 28px rgba(23,32,42,.05);display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center}.loop-stage>span{font-size:.68rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--accent-2)}.loop-stage strong{font-size:1.05rem;margin:.35rem 0}.loop-stage small{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.4}.listen{border-top:4px solid var(--teal)}.solve{border-top:4px solid var(--accent-2)}.enable{border-top:4px solid var(--gold)}.improve{border-top:4px solid var(--violet)}.retain{border-top:4px solid var(--teal)}.feedback-loop>i{font-style:normal;color:#9aabba;font-weight:900}.cx-highlight{margin-top:1.2rem;padding:1.35rem;border-radius:20px;background:linear-gradient(110deg,#0f766e,#176f81);color:#fff;display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:1.5rem;align-items:center}.cx-highlight span{display:block;font-size:.7rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#c6f1eb}.cx-highlight strong{display:block;font-size:1.35rem;line-height:1.2;margin-top:.2rem}.cx-highlight p{margin:0;color:#eefafa}.cx-evidence-section{background:#fff}.cx-card-grid .card{transition:transform .18s ease,box-shadow .18s ease}.cx-card-grid .card:hover{transform:translateY(-3px);box-shadow:0 15px 35px rgba(23,32,42,.08)}.fit-banner{display:grid;gap:.35rem;padding:1.2rem 1.3rem;border-radius:18px;background:var(--blue-soft);border-left:5px solid var(--accent-2)}.fit-banner strong{font-size:1.1rem}.fit-banner span{color:var(--ink)}.fit-banner small{color:var(--muted)}
  @media(max-width:1050px){.role-hero-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.lifecycle-panel{max-width:900px}.feedback-loop{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.feedback-loop>i{display:none}.cx-highlight{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  @media(max-width:800px){.cx-proof-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.lifecycle-track{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr}.lifecycle-track>i{display:none}.lifecycle-track>div{min-height:105px}.lifecycle-track>div:last-of-type{grid-column:2}.journey-proof{align-items:flex-start}}
  @media(max-width:600px){.role-hero{padding:3.4rem 0}.role-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,12vw,3.8rem)}.cx-proof-grid,.feedback-loop,.lifecycle-track{grid-template-columns:1fr}.lifecycle-track>div:last-of-type{grid-column:auto}.cx-proof-grid>div{border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.cx-proof-grid>div:last-child{border-bottom:0}.journey-proof{flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem}}
  @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.cx-card-grid .card{transition:none}.cx-card-grid .card:hover{transform:none}}
</style>
</BaseLayout>
